    "created_at": "2019-01-03T17:40:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-01-03T17:40:21Z",
    "body": "Sure, I was debating myself about whether the attribute should reflect the live value or not, but went with the simpler proposal.\r\n\r\nBut, I suppose: using a separate `defaultVolume` IDL avoids any performance impacts from live-update of the attribute (e.g., if volume is being continuously animated), and means that the attribute doesn't get added to the element unless the author specifically put it there, so it doesn't change existing behavior.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
